 "info": {
  "title": "tinyg-switchbox",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "summary": "Feather HUZZAH ESP8266 that opens and closes a CNC controller's limit/homing switch inputs electrically (TinyG v8 profile included).",
  "description": "Each channel is one ESP8266 GPIO wired to one switch input of a CNC controller such as a TinyG v8 (plus a common GND). It emulates an open-drain switch contact: `closed` sinks the line to GND, `open` leaves the pin high-Z so the controller's pull-up raises it. The pin is never driven high; inputs must be 3.3 V logic.\n\nA channel's `type` (`no`/`nc`) maps the semantic actions onto the contact: NO: trip = closed, release = open; NC: trip = open, release = closed. Ops accept either the contact level (`state`) or the semantic action (`action`).\n\nOne executor serves three transports with the same operations: newline-delimited JSON over the USB serial port (`x-serial-protocol`), this REST API, and a WebSocket at `/ws` (`x-websocket`). A serial or WebSocket request is `{\"id\":N,\"op\":\"<operationId>\",...params}`.\n\nEvery state change and every command that changes something (or fails) becomes an event with a sequence number and a 64-bit microsecond timestamp; successful read-only queries (get*) are not logged, so polling cannot evict history."
 },
 "servers": [
  {
   "url": "http://tinyg-switchbox.local",
   "description": "mDNS (station or AP mode)"
  },
  {
   "url": "http://192.168.4.1",
   "description": "fallback access point tinyg-switchbox-XXXX"
  }
 ],
